+# The Daily Grind account UI
+
+A static, responsive account screen with passkey listing, persistent preview edits, accessible rename/removal dialogs, and progressive WebAuthn Signal API synchronization.
+
+## Preview
+
+Open the site through the existing static hosting setup. The default is an explicitly labeled Jamie Davis preview account. Changes persist in this browser's local storage; Reset demo restores the three examples. Demo credentials are never sent to an authenticator. No authentication backend or real registered credentials were present in this repository.
+
+## Connect an authenticated account service
+
+Set `data-account-api="/api/account/passkeys"` on `<body>` and provide the session's CSRF token with `<meta name="csrf-token" content="…">`. The client uses same-origin credentials, disables response caching, and sends `X-CSRF-Token` on requests. These endpoints must be implemented by the account backend:
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`: return `{ rpId, userId, complete: true, credentials: [...] }`. The list must contain **all** credentials for the authenticated user, without pagination. `rpId` must match registration; `userId` must be the WebAuthn user handle, encoded as unpadded base64url.
+- Each credential: `{ id, name, registeredAt, lastUsedAt, provider, icon }`. IDs must be unpadded base64url; timestamps are epoch milliseconds (`lastUsedAt` may be null). Supply provider metadata resolved from registration AAGUID, with an unknown-provider fallback. Optional icon values: `laptop`, `phone`, `key`.
+- `PATCH /api/account/passkeys/:id`: accept `{ name }` (trimmed, 1–64 characters); return success or 204.
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`: delete only the authenticated user's credential; return success or 204. Prefer idempotent deletion so a retry after a lost response is safe.
+
+All endpoints must enforce authentication and credential ownership; mutation endpoints must verify CSRF tokens/origin and validate input server-side. Return 401 for expired sessions. Ensure the customer has a usable alternative sign-in method before removing a final passkey. Live mode never falls back to preview data on an API error. Replace the preview account identity/sidebar content with authenticated account data when integrating.
+
+On initial loading and after deletion, the client calls `signalAllAcceptedCredentials` using the complete server-provided list, RP ID, and user handle. It feature-detects the API and handles rejection without reversing a successful account update. Unsupported browsers show manual password-manager cleanup guidance. Renaming changes only the server nickname and does not rename a provider entry or call `signalCurrentUserDetails`.
+
+This task implements management of existing passkeys. Registration, sign-in, and account-profile mutations remain the responsibility of the site's authentication service. The current sidebar's secondary account views are preview content.
+
+## Checks
+
+Run `npm test` for persistence, authenticated API/error handling, Base64URL validation, and safe authenticator synchronization tests. No build step is required for this static site.
